{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Know surely.</b> He informed him of the cause for the delay in his children's taking possession — namely, <b>for the iniquity of the Amorite is not yet complete</b>, for it is not fitting to expel a nation from its land until its measure is full. He said: if so, know surely — that even though I have sworn to give the land to your children, this will not come about immediately, <b>for your seed shall be sojourners in a land not theirs</b> until that time when the iniquity of the Amorite reaches its completion. Together with this, He told of the events of the servitude and affliction destined then to befall some generations of his seed in their sufferings. For this did not happen to them in the generations of the righteous — as long as one of the tribes survived, the servitude did not begin — but it happened when they corrupted their way, as the prophet testified, saying (Ezekiel 20:8–9): וַיַּמְרוּ בִי וְלֹא אָבוּ לִשְׁמֹעַ אֵלַי וגו'. And all this He told so that a later generation may know by tradition that it is the word of HaShem, and not attribute the matter to another cause — as the prophet says (Isaiah 48:5): וָאַגִּיד לְךָ מֵאָז בְּטֶרֶם תָּבֹא וגו'."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The Hebrew לא יצחסו (the last word is pointed with a sin) means 'they will not attribute'; rendered accordingly. The verse citations in parentheses are editorial, not in the Hebrew text itself."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:19.812477170Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}